e less severe than C's unfriendly and not open to new ideas, which could hinder adaptability. So we could shift vote to B.\n\nWe should reference evidence: B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence). Concern: pretentious, sometimes wrong tone (crew cooperation). Compare to C's strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership, but unfriendly, not open to new ideas (crew cooperation, adaptability). We can argue that while C's technical strengths are strong, the attitude concerns are more severe for safety-critical teamwork. B's strengths in reliability and stress handling may outweigh his communication tone issues, which could be coached.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate B.\n\nWe need to include our own facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also note B's pretentiousness and tone issues.\n\nWe also might ask a tool question for missing criteria: e.g., ask Agent 1 about stress resilience for C or D, but we can proceed without.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nLet's craft: \"I appreciate Candidate C's technical insight, but I'm concerned about unfriendly attitude and lack of openness, which are critical for crew cooperation and adaptability. Candidate B shows strong reliability and stress handling, which are essential, and his communication issues seem less severe. Therefore I shift my provisional recommendation to Candidate B.\"\n\nInclude explicit facts.\n\nProceed."}
